rried away by Samson (Judges 16:1-3). Here he was afterwards a prisoner, and \"did grind in the prison house.\" Here he also pulled down the temple of Dagon, and slew \"all the lords of the Philistines,\" himself also perishing in the ruin (Judg. 16:21-30). The prophets denounce the judgments of God against it (Jeremiah 25:20 ; 47:5 ; Amos 1:6 Amos 1:7 ; Zephaniah 2:4). It is referred to in Acts 8:26 . Philip is here told to take the road from Jerusalem to Gaza (about 6 miles south-west of Jerusalem), \"which is desert\", i.e., the \"desert road,\" probably by Hebron, through the desert hills of Southern Judea. (See SAMSON .) It is noticed on monuments as early as B.C. 1600. Its small port is now called el-Mineh.","name_meaning":{"meaning":"strong","hebrew":"עַזָּה","translit":"azah","strongs":"H5804","greek":"Γάζα","greekTranslit":"Gáza","hitchcock":"strong; a goat"}},"geba_447":{"id":"geba_447","name":"Geba","kjvName":"Geba","esvName":"Geba","lat":31.85787804,"lon":35.25975522,"type":"City","aliases":[],"events":[],"peopleBorn":[],"peopleDied":[],"verses":[6317,6398,7488,9271,10173,10514,10581,11515,12053,12450,12619,12653,17879,23078],"verseCount":14,"name_meaning":{"meaning":"a hill; cup"}},"geba_448":{"id":"geba_448","name":"Geba","kjvName":"Geba","esvName":"Geba","lat":31.84684773,"lon":35.18491238,"aliases":[],"events":[],"peopleBorn":[],"peopleDied":[],"verses":[8157],"verseCount":1,"name_meaning":{"meaning":"a hill; cup"}},"gebal_449":{"id":"gebal_449","name":"Gebal","kjvName":"Gebal","esvName":"Gebal","lat":34.11910361,"lon":35.64614196,"type":"City","aliases":[],"events":[],"peopleBorn":[],"peopleDied":[],"verses":[8896,15248,21130],"verseCount":3,"name_meaning":{"meaning":"bound; limit"}},"gebim_450":{"id":"gebim_450","name":"Gebim","kjvName":"Gebim","esvName":"Gebim","lat":31.8,"lon":35.25,"aliases":[],"events":[],"peopleBorn":[],"peopleDied":[],"verses":[17881],"verseCount":1,"name_meaning":{"meaning":"grasshoppers; height"}},"geder_451":{"id":"geder